    "explanation": "# Release build: boundry-proof-core 0.1.2\n\nBuild, test and package release commit e01898148a6fedab290813debc95c18046ca26f5 for Boundry Maintenance release boundry-proof-core@0.1.2.\n\nRecipe `.boundry/recipes/boundry-release.md` · sha256:6bf500638088 · compiled by boundry-recipes/1.0.0 with boundry-capabilities/1.0.1 · definition d023cdcf601d\n\n## Runs when\n- an authorized person starts it\n\n## Project\n- Rust project (workspace) in the repository root (evidence: `Cargo.lock`, `Cargo.toml`)\n\n## Checks (one job)\n1. **The tests pass** — runs `cargo test --locked`\n   Rust (stable, with rustfmt and clippy) · installs dependencies first · internet: yes · keeps `test-results.txt` · capability `check.tests@1.0.0`\n\n## Steps (in order, after every check passes)\n1. **Package the crates** — runs `cargo package --locked --workspace` and collects the .crate files\n   Rust (stable, with rustfmt and clippy) · installs dependencies first · internet: yes · keeps `package.tar` · capability `step.package-crates@1.0.0`\n\n## Authority\n- Permissions: none\n- Secrets: none\n- Approvals: none\n- Publishes or deploys: nothing\n- Proposed changes from forks never receive secrets, release/deploy access or trusted caches.\n\n## Kept\n- `package.tar` from “Package the crates” for 3650 days\n- `test-results.txt` from “The tests pass” for 30 days (also when tests fail)\n- The record: this recipe, its compiled plan, project facts, every attempt's log, inputs and outputs (always)\n\n## Afterward\n- Nothing is reported to GitHub (add “Report the result on the change” to do so)\n",
